oad\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Authored held-out TDD oracle tests only (no src changes): added tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py and extended tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py. RED confirmed for missing seam imports and absent Terraform tools in code-review routing; negative-control no-tool cases pass as expected.","timestamp":1788546571827677284},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Design note (mechanism): code-review overlays receive per-prompt tools via the SHARED agent_runner provider seam (CodeReviewBatchRunner delegates each unit run to the passed agent_runner; batch_runner.py line ~92 'overlays follow the RUN's provider'), NOT a batch-runner-owned hook like plan-review's ProductionBatchRunner. So afe3 routes the Terraform seam via RunnerAgentStep.tool_provider (built by terraform_grounding.build_provider_and_sink from the assembled changed_files). The provider gates by prompt: code-review-iac (Round A/B) and code-review-verify get the two TF tools; base/coach/other overlays get none. changed_files also drives the externally-computed project_criteria passed into CodeReviewBatchRunner. Feature extracted to src/rebar/llm/code_review/terraform_grounding.py (152 LOC) to keep workflow_ops.py and gate_dispatch.py under the 800-LOC CI cap. All 7 ACs proven by held-out oracle (45 passed) through real production dispatch produce_code_review_verdict.","timestamp":1788556035746802001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788469523116095726,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8615cf0d-6693-4248-b195-0d4e583fe999","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"08ab-60d2-3082-4b47"},{"link_uuid":"913731fc-dc0d-481f-bf6c-37a974c6ec73","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8193-e0f3-9f88-4272"},{"link_uuid":"daffff4e-9fb5-472d-b5d4-baf24c38b624","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"},{"link_uuid":"8a2e97df-d6a8-4c41-8fe8-50461f7a9db4","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2d73-21d7-9965-42dc"},{"link_uuid":"1285d522-4be9-4a48-a321-4ee50530ae3e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d421-8a2f-431f-40cc"}],"description":"## Context\n\nCode review already routes changed Terraform to the `code-review-iac` overlay, but its Pass-1 overlay and Pass-2 verifier have only generic repository tools. This slice reuses the tool-session contract created by `forcible-diminished-lamb` [rebar:forcible-diminished-lamb] so IaC findings can cite and independently re-check whole-module evidence. It changes no behavior for other diffs.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Thread `assemble_diff.outputs.changed_files` into `CodeReviewBatchRunner`; its constructor already stores this field, but the production gate dispatcher currently omits it.\n- In both Round A and Round B, create a fresh Terraform tool session only for an included `code-review-iac` criterion when the changed set contains `.tf`, `.tf.json`, or an explicitly changed `.tfvars`. Supply the `lookup_declaration` and `resolve_reference` tools from the prerequisite. The base reviewer and every other overlay receive no Terraform tools.\n- Scope the session from changed paths, then use the prerequisite's whole affected-module/local-closure rules. A changed `.tfvars` remains direct evidence only and is never treated as an automatically selected input.\n- After Pass-1 merge, expose a new session to `code-review-verify` only when a merged finding is attributed to `code-review-iac` and the changed set has Terraform scope. The verifier receives the Pass-1 receipt as evidence but must issue its own query; there is no inherited answer or query ledger.\n- The coach and deterministic decision steps receive no Terraform tools.\n- Merge concrete/module-membership reads into the call's `_usage.distinct_fetches`. Include the concrete Terraform files read in the code-review sidecar's reviewed-file `deps` so region-gated re-review memory cannot reuse evidence after a module dependency changes.\n- Keep missing-extra behavior fail-open: code review continues through its existing generic path, with no advertised Terraform tools. An advertised tool failure returns the prerequisite's closed abstention and cannot itself create or block a finding.\n- Do not add a scanner stage or originate findings from the index. The IaC overlay remains the finder; grounding only answers its explicit queries.\n\n## Positive rationale\n\nThe slice is independently releasable after its prerequisite: a Terraform diff receives query-grounded IaC review end to end, while all non-IaC requests remain byte-compatible. It reuses the existing overlay routing and generic per-call tool-provider seam instead of creating a Terraform-specific review engine.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nNo new parser, source-network logic, corroborator executable, prompt change, standalone validation, Terraform/OpenTofu/provider execution, or non-IaC tool exposure.\n\n## Failure-disposition contract\n\n- Missing `grounding-terraform` extra: non-fatal capability absence; advertise no tools and complete the ordinary review.\n- Unsupported/ambiguous/dynamic Terraform question: return ABSTAIN; the LLM may verify directly from files but the tool supplies no positive claim.\n- Parser/path/limit/timeout failure: return ABSTAIN and preserve the existing review result; do not reinterpret it as a clean module or nonexistent symbol.\n- Internal routing/session construction defect: surface through existing gate error handling rather than silently attaching tools to a broader step.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Production dispatch passes the exact assembled `changed_files` into `CodeReviewBatchRunner`, and a Round-A changed-`.tf` integration test observes both Terraform tools only on `code-review-iac`.\n- [x] A Round-B escalation test observes the same tool surface and whole-module resolution when IaC is recommended rather than glob-selected, without running the overlay twice.\n- [x] A merged IaC finding makes `code-review-verify` receive a distinct Terraform query session; a verifier tool call returns a fresh receipt rather than reusing the Pass-1 result.\n- [x] Base review, non-IaC overlays, coach, a Python-only diff, and an IaC review with no IaC findings advertise no Terraform tools.\n- [x] A changed `.tfvars` can be queried as direct structural evidence, and a test proves its value is not injected into module variables or used to resolve a computed reference.\n- [x] Code-review usage and sidecar dependency tests contain the concrete sibling/local-module files read; modifying one invalidates the recorded dependency hash while an unrelated non-Terraform file does not.\n- [x] Missing-extra and every prerequisite ABSTAIN outcome leave the ordinary code-review decision path intact and never become a synthetic IaC finding.\n\n## Testing\n\nTest contract card:\n\n- Authoritative contract: REB-640, this ticket, and the prerequisite's tool/receipt contract [rebar:forcible-diminished-lamb].\n- Preconditions: a real assembled diff with one changed root `.tf`, an unchanged sibling declaration, a local child module, and captured Round-A/Round-B/verifier requests.\n- Production path: production gate dispatch → real `CodeReviewBatchRunner` → real tool session; only the model result is faked.\n- Tier: workflow integration, because the contract crosses trigger selection, overlay batch dispatch, merge, verifier routing, usage, and sidecar dependency capture.\n- Oracle: exact tool-name sets per request, distinct receipt/query-session ids across passes, resolved sibling evidence, and changed dependency digest after editing a read file.\n- Negative controls: an equivalent `.py` diff and a Terraform diff with no IaC finding leave base/other overlays/verifier/coach tool-free.\n- CI: `make test`.\n\n## Verification\n\n`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py`","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py","reason":"wire assembled changed_files + scoped Terraform tool provider into production code-review dispatch; fold grounding reads into verdict usage"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/terraform_grounding.py","reason":"new feature module: select IaC .tf/.tf.json-citing findings, gate on changed-set Terraform scope, build the per-prompt code-review Terraform tool provider+sink, fold grounding usage"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py","reason":"include concrete .tf grounding reads in reviewed-file dependency hashes"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py","reason":"Round-A/Round-B/Pass-2 routing and dependency integration oracle"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py","reason":"production code-review workflow byte-neutrality regression coverage"},{"path":"docs/grounding.md","reason":"document code-review Terraform grounding routing and failure behavior"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","08ab-60d2-3082-4b47"],["parent","a374-849c-c8f2-4234"],["relates_to","2d73-21d7-9965-42dc"],["relates_to","59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"],["relates_to","8193-e0f3-9f88-4272"],["relates_to","d421-8a2f-431f-40cc"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a374-849c-c8f2-4234","parent_status_uuid":"069a5e7f-02ea-42de-b7d3-4678ec3b0cb7","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"pr